.TH START-MU2EDAQ-HEARTBEATMONITOR.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-heartbeatmonitor t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
start\-mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor.sh \- start the heartbeat monitor daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B start\-mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor.sh
.RI [ config_file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Control\-room start script, run as
.BR "crs\-app start heartbeatmonitor" .
It changes to its own directory, exports
.B CRS_PORT_HTTP
(default 8081) and
.B CRS_PORT_UDP
(default 9999) if they are not already set, activates
.IR ./venv ,
and replaces itself with
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
python heartbeat_monitor.py \-\-config \fIconfig_file\fR \-\-daemon \e
    \-\-pid\-file <checkout>/heartbeat_monitor.pid
.fi
.RE
.PP
HTTP port 8081 is used because
.B mu2edaq\-resource\-manager
owns 8080.
.PP
The script does not check whether the monitor is already running.
A second start overwrites the PID file, fails on the HTTP port, and then
removes the PID file, leaving the first daemon running without one.
Use
.B "pgrep \-af heartbeat_monitor.py"
before starting by hand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I config_file
Configuration passed to
.BR \-\-config .
Default
.IR ./config/heartbeat_config.yaml .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./venv
Required; created by
.BR bootstrap_heartbeat_monitor.sh (1).
.TP
.I ./heartbeat_monitor.pid
PID file of the daemon.
.TP
.I /tmp/heartbeat_monitor.log
Daemon log (from
.B daemon.log_file
in the configuration).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CRS_PORT_HTTP
HTTP port; default 8081.
.TP
.B CRS_PORT_UDP
UDP heartbeat port for IPv4 and IPv6; default 9999.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 1
.I ./venv
does not exist.
.PP
Otherwise the exit status is that of the daemonizing parent, which is 0 once
it has forked.
A daemon that fails after forking, for example on a busy port, is not
reported; check the log.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS 4
.nf
\&./start\-mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor.sh
CRS_PORT_HTTP=8091 ./start\-mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor.sh config/test.yaml
curl \-s localhost:8081/api/health
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stop\-mu2edaq\-heartbeatmonitor.sh (1),
.BR heartbeat_monitor.py (1),
.BR bootstrap_heartbeat_monitor.sh (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ Group, Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory.
